task: subprocess-wire-depth-safety
agent: opus-depth
started: 2026-09-11
branch: feature/subprocess-wire-depth-safety
worktree: ../okay-wt-subprocess-depth
spec: found by a full-repo grep for Schema/Json recursion, at the
  operator's direct request ("поищи") following
  form-recursive-depth-safety

why: `okay-py/Py.scala`'s `Wire.enc`/`Wire.dec` and `okay-r/R.scala`'s
  `Wire.enc`/`Wire.dec` recurse natively on `PyValue.Arr`/`RValue.Vec`/
  `Json.JArr` depth — the exact defect shape `okay-mcp/Rpc.damaged`
  and `okay-demo/StateMcp.damaged` already had fixed twice (remove-
  codecs-maxdepth, encode-side-depth-safety): a plain recursive walk
  rebuilding a tree, no threshold. These bridge to a Python/R
  subprocess rather than raw network bytes — a lower-severity threat
  model (usually the same user's own process, not an internet
  attacker) but the same mechanism, and the operator asked to fix it
  regardless once found.

what: `Wire.enc`/`Wire.dec` in both files get the explicit work-list
  rewrite `Rpc.damaged`/`StateMcp.damaged` already got — these are
  simple tree-rebuilding recursions (no monadic combination to
  preserve), so an explicit-stack iterative rewrite is the right
  weight, not a full Cont.defer trampoline.

  Audited and found SAFE, not touched: `okay-conf/Conf.scala`
  (explicitly flat by design), `okay-r/R.scala`'s frame decode/encode
  (docstring: "no nesting inside a data.frame column"),
  `okay-intent/Classify.scala` (schema-only recursion, no paired
  value of external-controlled depth), `okay-sql/Typed.scala`,
  `okay-ui/Protocol.scala`, `okay-cluster/Wire.scala`,
  `okay-crdt/Wire.scala`, `okay-script/Serve.scala` (schema-definition
  or schema-only walks, no value-depth risk).

predict: small, mechanical — two functions per file, four total,
  matching an already-landed pattern exactly. Needs tests building a
  deep PyValue/RValue directly (not through any subprocess) proving
  enc/dec round-trip at depth without native stack overflow.
